  "body": "Section 13.2.3.5 says that U+000D must be removed from the input stream. If this is not done, then the character U+000D will be added to the current tag token's tag name in step 13.2.5.8 (Tokenizer tag name state) for example (<a\\r\\nhref=\"#\"> will result in the tag name \"a\\r\"). Why do we check this symbol at the tree construction stage if it was removed earlier?\r\n\r\n> 13.2.3.5 Preprocessing the input stream\r\n> Before the tokenization stage, the input stream must be preprocessed by normalizing newlines. Thus, newlines in HTML DOMs are represented by U+000A LF characters, and there are never any U+000D CR characters in the input to the tokenization stage.\r\n\r\n> 13.2.6 Tree construction\r\n> A character token that is one of U+0009 CHARACTER TABULATION, U+000A LINE FEED (LF), U+000C FORM FEED (FF), U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR), or U+0020 SPACE",
